# REGRESSION (was todo/t0840, found while widening its net): a SINGLE-OWNER
# opaque handle at a consuming position.
#
# `Mutex[T]` is a `GorgetMutex*` typedef with a drop and NO clone path. Once
# the element slot actually held the handle (the t0840 write repair), `m` and
# the collection slot both owned it and both dropped: `free(): double free
# detected in tcache 2`, both backends. Before that repair the cell "passed"
# only because the slot held garbage the drop happened to survive — the
# `Vector[Mutex]` was never usable at all (Core #15e Q6: a green cell green for
# an unrelated reason).
#
# The repair is the CoW contract's own rule — owns AND dead at this call ⇒
# move — applied to the handles `is_resource_type` answers `false` for because
# their `copy_semantics` is `Trivial` (`is_single_owner_handle_local`).
# Refcount handles are excluded: they incref at the boundary and both owners
# drop legitimately.
#
# CELL: container=Vector · handle=Mutex · payload=int · producing-arm=push ·
#       read=`.get(i).unwrap().lock().get()`.

void main():
    Mutex[int] m = Mutex[int](5)
    Vector[Mutex[int]] all = []
    all.push(m)
    print(f"{all.len()}")
    print(f"{all.get(0).unwrap().lock().get()}")
